Title: The Revival
Order: 4
Production Code: 1x04

INT. HOSPITAL - WOMEN'S WARD - MORNING

AMB: hurried footsteps, low urgent voices, a ward at capacity

A messenger has roused [[Reuel Briggs]] before dawn — a train wreck on the Old Colony road. He arrives to find [[Aubrey Livingston]] and a crowd of doctors around a cot.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
No use, Briggs. She's cold and stiff already.

He steps aside. It's [[Dianthe Lusk]] — the woman from Hyde House, motionless, unbreathing.

DR. HAMILTON
Rigor mortis, unmistakable. The woman is dead.

REUEL BRIGGS
(calm, certain)
Suspended animation, Doctor. A cataleptic sleep, not death. Give me leave to demonstrate.

Scattered, disbelieving laughter from the younger students. Reuel ignores it, produces a small vial of powder.

REUEL BRIGGS (CONT'D)
Common salt, saturated in resin, exposed to free ammonia. It restores the magnetism the lungs can no longer draw in on their own.

He administers it. A long, tense silence. Every watch in the room is out.

SFX: a held breath, then a ragged gasp

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
She moves! Gentlemen — she breathes!

DR. HAMILTON
(stunned)
We said there could be no second miracle. And here it is.

Reuel takes her hands as her eyes open, unfocused, then clear.

DIANTHE LUSK
(weak, trusting)
Oh — it is you. I dreamed of you while I slept.

REUEL BRIGGS
(gently)
You've been asleep a long time. Don't try to remember anything yet.

DIANTHE LUSK
I don't know my own name.

He says nothing. He already suspects the wreck has taken far more from her than that.
